# Code review lessons (read before changing scheduler, radio, auth, or tests)

Historical fix notes that were never filed as GitHub issues: `docs/code-review-findings.md`. Do not add bugs or minor enhancements there, or anywhere else in the repo, once they are GitHub issues. When you file an issue, delete the local note that only described it.

Add a one-line lesson here only when a fix reveals a pattern that would be easy to repeat in this codebase.

## Scheduler (`app/scheduler.py`)
- Decide what to schedule or prune by **`fire_at`**, never by the slot center (:00/:30). Overlays fire up to ±`slot_half_window_minutes` from the center.
- Never re-add an APScheduler `DateTrigger` whose time has passed: inside the misfire grace it runs again (double transmission). Only add future jobs; keep a past one only if it still exists.
- Busy-retry (`defer:`) jobs live until their own `deadline_iso`; do not prune them by slot window.
- Manual triggers never change slot jobs — don't call `sync_jobs()` from that path.

## Radio / DRA
- USB unplug aborts **in-flight transmit** (lead + PCM), not the app — use `begin_usb_transmit`/`end_usb_transmit`, interruptible `aplay`, and `TransmitAbortError`; skip COS poll HID work while HID absent.
- PTT: track each device as soon as it keys; on any failure unkey exactly those. A stuck PTT is the worst failure mode.
- Multiple PortAudio streams: never write a whole buffer to one stream before the next — `write()` blocks. Interleave short blocks (`write_programs_interleaved`).
- HTTP handlers must not sample COS or reschedule jobs; that belongs to the background COS thread.

## Config, data, auth
- `app/config.py` reads env at import; tests set `TTS_SKIP_DOTENV=1`. Never let a developer `.env` affect tests.
- Never treat an unrecognized data file as empty — raise `DataFileError`; a later save would erase data.
- Timer-driven UI requests send an `X-Background-Poll` header so they don't defeat the idle logout. The server checks only that it is present — don't add a magic value that must match between Python and JS. Tests use `app.auth.BACKGROUND_POLL_HEADER`.
- Home live status uses SSE (`/api/events/home`); terminal transitions (running cleared, manual trigger finished) must publish with `force=True` or other tabs can keep stale pending state until the 15 s REST refresh.
- Manual trigger status: report the radio phase (busy / clear-hold countdown) even while a retry is in flight — retries spend most of their time blocked in the clear wait. "In progress" is not a useful UI state.
- COS: never debounce busy samples — a kerchunk is often a single 0.25 s sample and must reset the clear hold. Missed HID reads are "no reading", not busy; handle them there.
- The last COS check before PTT must read COS fresh (`_confirm_clear_before_ptt`). `channel_blocks_transmit` skips the read once idle credit meets the hold — never use it as the final gate.
- Dependencies live in `pyproject.toml` + `uv.lock`, managed with `uv add` / `uv add --dev` / `uv remove`. Never `pip install` into the venv or hand-write `requirements.txt` (it is generated by `uv export` for deploys and gitignored). Run tests with `uv run pytest`.
- The version lives only in `pyproject.toml` (bump with `uv version --bump ...`). `app.__version__` reads it via `importlib.metadata`; never hardcode a version (e.g. FastAPI `version=`) or add a second copy.
- Stub mode never goes busy and transmits instantly; verify trigger/queue/playing UI on the NUC with `TTS_RADIO_BACKEND=dra`.
- One source of defaults: env/config → `/api/voices` → UI. Don't hard-code defaults in `static/app.js`.
- Slot math uses `Settings.timezone` only; `Schedule.timezone` is legacy.

## Tests
- Run the full suite (`pytest`) before finishing; it must pass with and without a `.env`.
- New behavior fix ⇒ a regression test that fails on the old code.
- Server startup replaces the radio; tests rely on the `keep_test_radio` autouse fixture.
